   "source": [
    "# 6. Real Life Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means clustering is widely used in many real-world applications.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Customer Segmentation\n",
    "Companies use K-Means to group customers according to:\n",
    "- purchasing behavior,\n",
    "- age,\n",
    "- interests,\n",
    "- spending habits.\n",
    "\n",
    "This helps businesses create targeted marketing campaigns.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Recommendation Systems\n",
    "Streaming and e-commerce platforms use clustering to recommend:\n",
    "- movies,\n",
    "- music,\n",
    "- products,\n",
    "- videos\n",
    "\n",
    "to users with similar preferences.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "Users who watch similar movies may receive similar recommendations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Image Compression\n",
    "K-Means is used to reduce the number of colors in an image.\n",
    "\n",
    "This helps:\n",
    "- reduce image size,\n",
    "- optimize storage,\n",
    "- improve transmission speed.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Medical Analysis\n",
    "Hospitals and researchers use clustering to:\n",
    "- group patients with similar symptoms,\n",
    "- identify disease patterns,\n",
    "- analyze medical records.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Market Analysis\n",
    "Businesses use clustering to identify:\n",
    "- market trends,\n",
    "- customer categories,\n",
    "- product preferences.\n",
    "\n",
    "This supports strategic decision-making.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Social Network Analysis\n",
    "Social media platforms use clustering to:\n",
    "- detect communities,\n",
    "- identify groups of users with similar interests,\n",
    "- analyze user interactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Fraud Detection\n",
    "Banks and financial institutions use clustering to detect unusual transactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Transactions that do not belong to normal clusters may indicate fraudulent activity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90d61458",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7. Limitations and Challenges\n",
    "\n",
    "Although K-Means is simple and efficient, it also presents several limitations and challenges.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Sensitive to Outliers\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means uses the mean position of points to compute centroids.\n",
    "Because of this, extreme values (outliers) can significantly affect centroid positions.\n",
    "\n",
    "As a result:\n",
    "- clusters may become distorted,\n",
    "- centroid locations may shift incorrectly,\n",
    "- clustering quality may decrease.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Requires Selecting the Number of Clusters in Advance\n",
    "\n",
    "The user must specify the number of clusters \\( K \\) before training the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Choosing an inappropriate value for \\( K \\) can lead to:\n",
    "- over-clustering,\n",
    "- under-clustering,\n",
    "- poor data separation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Methods such as the Elbow Method are often used to estimate an appropriate number of clusters.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Performs Poorly on Non-Spherical Clusters\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means assumes that clusters are approximately spherical and equally distributed.\n",
    "\n",
    "When clusters have:\n",
    "- irregular shapes,\n",
    "- varying densities,\n",
    "- overlapping regions,\n",
    "\n",
    "the algorithm may incorrectly assign points to clusters.\n",
    "\n",
    "Algorithms such as DBSCAN are often more suitable for such datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Sensitive to Centroid Initialization\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial positions of centroids strongly influence the final clustering result.\n",
    "\n",
    "Poor initialization may cause:\n",
    "- slow convergence,\n",
    "- unstable clustering,\n",
    "- suboptimal solutions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The K-Means++ initialization strategy helps reduce this problem by selecting better initial centroids.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## May Converge to Local Minima\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means does not always find the global optimal solution.\n",
    "\n",
    "Depending on initialization, the algorithm may converge to a local minimum instead of the best clustering configuration.\n",
    "\n",
    "For this reason, K-Means is often executed multiple times with different random initializations.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Difficulty Handling Clusters with Different Sizes\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means performs best when clusters have similar sizes and densities.\n",
    "\n",
    "If one cluster is much larger or denser than another, the algorithm may produce inaccurate boundaries between groups.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Not Suitable for Categorical Data\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means relies on Euclidean distance, which is designed for numerical data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the algorithm is generally not appropriate for:\n",
    "- text categories,\n",
    "- labels,\n",
    "- non-numerical attributes."
   ]
  },
